Fillets: an OnSame end whose section is an edge of the face at the end,
the corner face before it consumed (mitcad#342).

A boss 1.5 high on a wall, its long top edges rounded with 2 (the rounding
rolls on the foot edges), the feet of those roundings rounded with 2, the
ends' edges with the roundings rounded with 1.5; then the ends' feet are
rounded with 2, the radius of the foot roundings beside them. At each corner
the ball fits the foot rounding: the end section is that rounding's end arc,
from the corner's vertex on the wall to the arc's other end, where the
opposite contact (on the corner rounding of the boss's top beyond) ends.
The corner torus between them (the foot rounding's corner, 0.5 wide) lies
wholly between the contacts and is consumed; the blend is tangent to it and
to the foot rounding all along the arc. OCCT took the torus for the face at
the end (OnSame) and intersected the blend with it, which is singular along
the arc, and the corner failed ("echec calcul intersection").

- ChFi3d_EndSectionAlongEdge, in PerformOneCorner's OnSame end once the
  edge to prolong (Arcprol) is found: the point on the blend's own side at
  the corner's vertex, the opposite point at the other vertex of Arcprol,
  the section between them on Arcprol's curve, the face at the end not one
  of the blend's faces and its other edges on the spine or shared with the
  opposite face. The face beyond Arcprol is then the face at the end, and
  the end is built as one whose section lies in that face (0410): the cap is
  Arcprol's own curve from one point to the other (its curves on the blend
  and on that face with the same parametrisation), its points the two
  vertices on no arc, the spine's edge cut at the vertex. No prolongation
  of the opposite contact is made: it ends at Arcprol's vertex.
- The cap takes Arcprol's place on the face at the end (with Arcprol's
  orientation there), and the consumed face goes: its edges off the spine,
  Arcprol among them, are cut at their vertices, so that the builder drops
  them with it (as ChFi3d_CutConsumedFaces drops consumed strips).

The new faces join the foot roundings tangentially along their arcs, as the
bodies of a stored design that has this corner do (its blend faces within
0.002 mm2 of the stored ones).

Upstream: new.
